# .cursor context (FADE)

Orient token-consciously at task start. List `.cursor/` if unsure; open only what the task needs.

| Path | When |
|------|------|
| `agent-docs/AGENTS.md` | Always first — architecture hub |
| `agent-docs/SCRIPT_INDEX.md` | Any `.sqf` / networking change (update on script edits) |
| `agent-docs/AGENTS_EDEN.md` | Eden object names, boards, textures |
| `agent-docs/AGENTS_PATTERNS.md` | GUIs, hints, MP, spawning |
| `agent-docs/AGENTS_REFERENCE.md` | Mission types, scenario GUI, BIS/RPT |
| `rules/` | When adding or editing Cursor rules |
| `skills/*/SKILL.md` | When user task matches skill description |
| `../tools/` (mpmissions sibling) | Only when task or user points at a helper |

Most of `.cursor/` is gitignored. **`rules/`** and **`skills/`** stay tracked and shareable.
